<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31341" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nūcĕrĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of several cities</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city in Campania</i>, with the appellation
			Alfaterna, the modern <i>Nocera</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 9, 41,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">23,
			15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Agr. 2, 31, 86</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Balb. 11, 28</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nūcĕ-rīnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŭc-</span></b> ,
					<i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 26, 517</span></i>), a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Nuceria, Nucerian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
					38</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nū-cĕrīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the Nucerians</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city in Umbria</i>, now <i>Nocera,
				whose inhabitants are called</i> Nucerini Favonienses <i>and</i> Camelani, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14,
				19, § 114</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
